interface_review = "This slice produces no registered interface. The 55 explorer route rows, including both health mounts and metadata PATCH, were compared with backend mounts, reqwest construction and nested response models. REST path parameters are encoded, filters use query fields, CAPTCHA uses JSON, and raw status/body survive 4xx/5xx. Response/cursor disagreements are findings. The eth_sign row is embedded vendored commentary, not an executable consumer. Auxiliary Celestia bindings describe an external service rather than a node namespace."
lifecycle_review = "Rust clients retain shared configuration/HTTP connections with no durable chain, tenant or pagination checkpoint. Reads can repeat after restart; absent cursor support prevents complete traversal. Metadata PATCH delegates refresh to existing backend CAPTCHA/protection and refresh lifecycle with no client success persistence. SQL sandbox fixtures roll back test state; unsafe global cache restart ownership is a finding. There is no in-scope migration, background indexer or program ABI registration."
security_review = "No in-scope code introduces node signing or a receipt-verification bypass. Public REST reads and backend metadata-refresh protection stay on mounted producer paths; the client sends CAPTCHA JSON. Credential Debug exposure and unbounded default transport are findings. Historical Solidity/compiler fixtures describe data to verify, not live deployment choices."
review_limit = "Static source/interface/documentation audit with explicit generated and vendored dispositions. Declared gates validate the record and task graph only; they do not run Elixir/Rust integration tests, contact production, prove dependency remediation or establish upgrade readiness."

